[? if f_capital = 0 : The sierra takes you back the way it takes back everything — without comment. The war is not over; you are only, once again, small. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# LA NEGOCIACIÓN — the prize of a win. The state, its authority in question, comes to the table.
# =====================================================================
@la_negociacion
title: La negociación
new-page: true
face-image: img/congreso.jpg
subtitle: A cracked authority sends an emissary — and now the hard part begins

= La negociación

You did the thing the manuals said could not be done on this ground, and the state has done the thing states do when their authority is publicly broken: it has sent someone to talk. A man with soft hands and a portfolio arrives under a flag of truce in the plaza you took, and he does not threaten, because threats are for governments that still believe they are winning. He *offers.* Amnesty. The Party's registration. Land reform in Guerrero, real this time, with the cameras watching. A place at a table that has never had a chair for people like you.

It is the most dangerous moment of the whole war — more dangerous than the cerco, than the assault — because it is the moment the revolution decides what it actually wanted. The gun won you a hearing. What you do with the hearing is the only question that was ever really being asked.

[? if pol_pcm < 20 and pol_intl < 25 : **Nobody vouches for you.** With no channel to the Party and no witnesses abroad, the man with the portfolio has come to *measure* you, not to sign. A movement with no political face cannot cash a military victory — it can only keep fighting until someone finally wins. ?][? if pol_pcm >= 55 : *The Party is at the table with you: its lawyers, its legality, its national name — the terms are real, and there is somebody to convert this into power.* ?][? if pol_intl >= 45 : *And the world is watching this room, which is why the offer is generous and why it will be honoured.* ?]

- @neg_apertura: **Tomar la apertura.** Trade the gun for the opening: amnesty, registration, the reforms — and carry the victory and its legend down into the political road, where a movement that took a capital cannot be rounded to zero. *(end the foco victorious; the political side becomes far stronger)*
- @neg_doble: **Reforma con fusil.** Take the reforms and keep the guns — trust nothing, disarm nothing, hold the ground you won as insurance against the accord being broken the way accords always are. *(partial political gain; you stay armed, and the state may betray)*
- @neg_seguir: **No parar.** Refuse. The state is on its knees — press the advantage, take more of Guerrero, let the example spread before the giant to the north can decide what to do about it. *(keep fighting; U.S. intervention risk climbs)*

@neg_apertura
choose-if: pol_pcm >= 20 or pol_intl >= 25
unavailable-subtitle: No channel to the Party, no witnesses abroad — nobody will guarantee an accord with you, and the state will not sign one it can break for free.
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.f_negociado=1; Q.f_phase="despues"; Q.via="politica"; Q.postura_guerrilla=0;
Q.veteranos=(Q.veteranos||0)+3; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+8; Q.registro=(Q.registro<1?1:Q.registro);
Q.legitimidad_regimen-=6; Q.pri_reformist_rel=(Q.pri_reformist_rel||0)+18; Q.fe_voto=(Q.fe_voto||0)+18; var _pb=Math.round((Q.pol_pcm||0)/10); Q.unity=(Q.unity||0)+_pb; Q.political_capital=(Q.political_capital||0)+_pb; Q.organizers=(Q.organizers||0)+Math.round((Q.pol_pcm||0)/25); Q.fe_voto+=Math.round((Q.pol_intl||0)/8);
Q.sup_peasants=(Q.sup_peasants||0)+10; Q.apoyo_sierra_gob=1; Q.unity=(Q.unity||0)+8;
!}

You come down out of the mountains with your rifles slung and your backs straight, and it is not a surrender — a surrender is what happens to the defeated, and you took a capital. It is a *transaction*, made from the one position of strength the Mexican left has never once held: the state needed the war to end more than you did. The amnesty is signed. The Party is registered. The land in Guerrero moves, and the campesinos who fed you for three years watch their sons walk out of the ejido with the caciques unable to touch them, because there is a movement behind the boy now, and the movement has proven it will fight.

The foco is over. What walks down from the sierra into the political road is not a defeated band accepting mercy but a victorious one collecting a debt — veterans who have seen the worst, a legend that organizes the south for a generation, and the one thing two decades of legal struggle never bought: the country's knowledge that this movement, cornered, does not break. Everything you build from here, you build stronger.

- @root: Bajar a la política. Continuar.

@neg_doble
